WEBVTT

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.960
What's that sound?

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.250
Ms. Ryu...?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.540
Not again. 

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.880
It's exactly the same. That thing... it's coming...

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.960
Oh... Alise...

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.830
H-hey, so...

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.460
Run away.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.170
Huh?

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.710
You have to run!

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.380
Hurry and get away!

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.420
At the very least you have to escape! Get out of here!

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.670
Hurry up!

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.130
Too late!

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.170
We're in the presence of despair!

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.170
Yes! Come on!

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.670
Show yourself to everyone!

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:00.170
One more time! Let us see it up close!

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.000
A great disaster... cometh.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.630
Take heed. 

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.080
It is a banquet of tragedy. 

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:44.290
Is it Wrong to Try to Pick Up Girls in a Dungeon?  IV

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:51.170
Ubugoe ga agatta sono hi kara bokura mina ichiyou ni

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:55.670
Aomuke ni koronde sora o aoideitakke

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.920
Kimi no me ni utsutta shoukei no iro ga fukumaru hodo

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.920
Toonoite iku kimi o zutto miteita

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.000
Yume ni egaki tsuzuketeita mono ga

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:14.330
Hai ni nate kieru toshitemo

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:19.210
Soredemo kimi wa susunde yuke

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:23.250
Inotteiru yo

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:29.880
Akaku akaku ibitsu ni moeteiru

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.670
Mune no okusoko de chiisaku yureugoku hi ga

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:43.750
Sora o egaita shounen wa akogare no mama ni habataita

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:48.000
Kazoekirenai kizu to tomo ni

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.880
Juggernaut

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.880
The Destroyer

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:04.330
No... I hate this sound!

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:06.630
I'm scared...

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.630
So scared... so scared!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.250
I know about it...

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:18.000
They said that something very terrifying happens
whenever you hear this sound.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.130
What is this sound?

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.670
It's almost like the dungeon is screaming out in anguish...

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.380
It seems like it's coming from somewhere below.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.290
Maybe the 27th floor?

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.880
Do you have any ideas, Lady Aisha?

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:37.750
Nope.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.880
First time I've heard this sound.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.170
Cassandra!

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:46.880
Pull it together!

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.960
Out of here...

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:53.920
Huh?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:56.710
Get out of here.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.500
Wh-what the hell?

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.330
I've never heard anything like this before.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.750
We should get off this floor ASAP. This is bad news!

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.040
C'mon, Bors!

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.210
It stopped...

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:37.750
It can't be!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.170
What's going on, Ouranos?

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.000
That thing has spawned!

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.130
"Thing"? What are you talking about?

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.420
I can't believe it's happening again.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:52.540
It will be an awful tragedy just like before.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.420
What are you talking about, Ouranos?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.000
Ouranos!

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.500
A disaster has just been reborn.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.130
What was that?

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.000
Something doesn't feel right.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.790
We gotta hurry and find Bors' group.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:20.750
Let's move.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.080
Did you hear that?

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:05.920
Yeah...

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.170
What is going on?

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:09.790
Time to go.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:11.460
W-wait, Bors!

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.330
Hurry up!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.000
My gut says we're in deep shit.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.380
What is happening?!

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.290
Is this because of you? Tell me!

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.960
What have you done?!

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.380
Just a ritual!

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:34.250
One that's gonna wake me up from this living nightmare.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:35.790
Huh?

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:40.250
Seeing Lion act like that hasn't
tipped you off yet, Bell Cranel?

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.210
Huh?

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:45.790
I summoned a monster.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:49.920
It's the same one that butchered
the Astrea Familia all those years ago!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.630
And it's coming here to the 27th floor!

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.250
The Astrea Familia?

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.500
That's the group that Ms. Ryu used to belong to.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.830
Five years ago,

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:07.920
the members of the Astrea Familia were constantly
fighting against those of us in the Rudra Familia.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:11.130
For them it was a crusade of justice or some crap,

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:15.420
but to us they were nothing but pesky flies
who kept getting in the damn way.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.380
So we set a trap in the dungeon to get rid of 'em!

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:21.880
You bastard!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.880
This reminds me, when I met with Ms. Ryu on the 18th
floor...

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.580
Ms. Ryu, what is this place?

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:34.080
The grave of my companions from
the Familia to which I once belonged.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.040
We fell into a trap set in the dungeon
by an enemy Familia.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:41.330
And all but I...

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.830
were killed.

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:58.080
That means... this guy is responsible
for the death of her Familia!

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:03.380
It was the same back then. We stocked up on all
the blazerocks that we could get our hands on.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.790
We lured Lion's Familia into the dungeon
intending to blow it up

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.290
and leave them buried alive under all the rubble!

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:13.830
Except, those assholes from
the Astrea Familia just wouldn't die!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.750
They survived like goddamn cockroaches!

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.250
That turned the tables and
put us in a really bad situation.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:20.880
But...

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:24.500
Something happened that
none of us could have foreseen!

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:25.920
And what was that?

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.130
The dungeon gave birth to an abomination!

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:36.750
A totally insane monster that no one
had seen or even heard of before!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.830
Normally, nothing like this should occur.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.330
Adventurers destroying a part
of the dungeon is inconsequential.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:56.000
It should only prompt the dungeon to begin
restoring itself back to its normal state.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:00.130
However, if the damage exceeds what it can repair...

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:04.540
Or rather, if someone made it a point to inflict
an overwhelming amount of damage...

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:05.960
Exactly.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:09.750
The dungeon would then prioritize eliminating
that "someone" over anything else.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:13.210
Excessive damage triggers its self-preservation instincts.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.130
And the dungeon suffers so much misery from this...

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.500
that not even my prayers can reach it.

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:24.460
Then what happened 5 years ago... will happen again.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.830
I'm afraid so.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:36.170
On that day... all of my allies were
slaughtered until only I was left.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:38.880
But guess what!

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:42.830
So were all of those stupid bitches
from the Astrea Familia!

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:48.000
I spent these past 5 years studying it.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:53.710
Those guys from Evilus that I hung around with
had no idea, because I did it all by my lonesome!

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:59.880
What triggered the dungeon to spawn it? And what
would I need to make that abomination appear again?

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:02.000
I studied it down to the last detail!

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:02.670
Huh?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.920
And oh boy, did I learn a lot!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.790
Like the fact that going beyond the middle floors

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:13.250
and intentionally causing a staggering amount of
damage to the dungeon on a lower floor

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:17.250
would then spawn the monster on that very same floor!

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:24.830
Also, the crucial fact that the dungeon can perceive
floors 25 through 27 as one single whole!

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.290
Cheer up, Lion.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:34.210
You have the honor of seeing the fruits of
my research as I announce them to the world!

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.380
Damn you, Jura!

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:40.250
Why?!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:45.130
Why would you want to summon a horrific monster
like that a SECOND time?!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.210
Isn't that obvious?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.880
Because I'm going to tame it!

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.960
Tame it? You can't be serious.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:56.290
Are you completely out of your mind?!

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.630
Tell me something, Lion.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:02.920
When you saw it for the first time,
did you think that it was a monstrosity?

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:04.750
Well, not me.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:10.460
Even though I was shitting and pissing myself
in sheer terror, I found myself mesmerized by it!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.330
By the way it laid waste to everything!

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.710
By the way it totally butchered everyone!

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:23.290
In my eyes, it was a thing of such beauty that even
goddesses pale in comparison! And I fell in love with it!

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:26.880
A being of overwhelming power!

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:30.210
I want it! I NEED it!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.380
ALL FOR MYSELF!

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:35.210
You're insane! That thing is practically the devil itself!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.580
There's absolutely no way that you can control it!

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.580
In normal circumstances, sure!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.080
But look...

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.130
I have this baby!

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:49.500
Oh right! He used that to control the Lambton!

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:51.420
It's a magic item!

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:58.130
Once I have control of that thing,
then nothing will scare me anymore!

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.830
And nobody can threaten me again!

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:03.170
Not even you, Lion!

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.750
I haven't gone a single day
without you haunting my dreams...

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.960
But summoning that creature here will change that.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.420
I'll finally be able to overcome the trauma of my past!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:18.040
I won't let anyone else have it!

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:22.290
IT WILL BE MINE!

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.250
We can't tell what's going on down there from here.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.710
What's the matter, Lady Chigusa?

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.540
I just heard someone...

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:03.000
They were screaming in pain...

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:10.040
Are you sure about that, Lady Chigusa?

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:11.500
P-pretty sure.

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.250
It was very faint, but I also heard it.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.170
Seemed to me like it was the cry
of an adventurer biting the dust.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:23.670
That settles it. Something must be
happening down on the 27th floor.

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:26.040
Do you think Master Bell has been swept up in it?

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.210
Hold on, Lil Squeak!

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.130
Come on, you guys! Let's go down there!

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.210
Master Bell needs our help right now!

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:40.460
Cassandra?

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.670
What are you doing, Lady Cassandra?!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:44.790
Please let me go!

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.420
We don't have time to waste!

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:51.040
I'm sorry... I'm so sorry...

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:54.250
I knew...

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.170
I knew that a disaster was looming...

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:00.330
But I couldn't do anything!

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:07.130
And because you guys are alive right now,
I'm sure that down on the 27th floor...

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:10.290
many other people are dying instead.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.250
I'm sorry!

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.790
I'm sorry!

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.670
I'm sorry!

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:23.750
I can feel it.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.290
It's already started.

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:30.420
I'm scared! So scared!

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:32.540
I want to run.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.580
Go far away.

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:37.000
Somewhere deep within the waters.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:56.880
I want to be with him.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.420
With Bell. Right now.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.210
Bell!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.500
Where are you?!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.500
A taboo of the dungeon that no one is aware of.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:12.960
Making it an official regulation is difficult.

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:18.000
Because, inversely, doing so would make
everyone aware of that thing's existence.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:25.380
We had no choice but to cover up any incident related
to it and never disclosed anything to the public.

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:31.420
Naturally, there is absolutely no information
about it in the Guild's records, either.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:35.460
However, there is one exception. The Xenos.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:41.330
Five years ago, they could sense that something
was very wrong and were more terrified than anyone.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.380
So I told them everything.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:50.330
And asked for their assistance in making sure
that nothing like this would ever happen again.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.750
But now, in a case of awful timing,

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:57.420
they are busy helping us to seize
complete control over Knossos.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:00.670
Yes.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:03.210
We have no way to respond to this swiftly.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.790
It seems to be located on the middle floors...

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.920
No, the lower floors.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:11.130
My god! Are the ones who happened to be in its path...

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.290
the Hestia Familia?!

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:20.330
So there's a monster powerful enough
to wipe out Ms. Ryu's entire Familia,

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:23.080
and you seriously just summoned it to this floor?!

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.290
Mr. Bors!

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:29.920
Wait!

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:33.130
But Ms. Ryu! We need to hurry and
save the other adventurers down here!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.250
It's impossible.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:36.630
You can't go out there.

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:40.170
Fighting it is a death sentence...

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.130
Of course!

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:49.170
It makes sense that you wouldn't let him go, Lion!

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.920
You know even more than I do
about how horrific that thing is,

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.710
since you got to experience fighting against it firsthand!

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:00.830
And let's not forget, you were so desperate
to keep yourself alive during that battle

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:05.960
that you let all your precious little friends
die without even trying to help!

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:07.630
Shut up.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.460
Oh, my mistake.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:13.880
You actually just outright slaughtered all your friends with
your own two hands!

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.210
SHUT UP!

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.080
SHUT UP! SHUT UP!

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:19.000
SHUT UP! SHUT UP!

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.500
Shut up! Shut up... Shut up... Shut up...

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:28.830
Shut up...

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:45.580
S-stay away!

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.250
The name of this disastrous fiend is "Juggernaut".

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:13.210
A destroyer that massacres any
and all adventurers it finds.

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:15.460
H-help...

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.630
Isn't there anything that we can do, Ouranos?

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:23.880
No matter what we do, it will be too late.

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:28.630
That thing will keep going until it's killed everyone
who happens to be in that area.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.540
That's the entire purpose of its existence.

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:42.420
Just you wait, precious.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.330
I'm going to make you mine soon enough!

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:49.290
Bring it on! You won't get me that easil-!

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:55.460
Big bro!

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.540
NO!

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.170
DAMMIT!

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.130
Hang on, Mr. Bors!

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:22.920
Mr. Cranel!

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.750
THAT'S ENOUGH!

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.040
Rabbit's Foot!

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.330
It hardly has any armor.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:51.000
That means it's a monster built for speed and offense!

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:52.960
I can handle that!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.040
It all comes down to striking first!

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:06.960
Where'd it go?!

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:14.170
Impossible. It moved that far in the blink of an eye?!

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.460
It's as strong as a Floor Boss...

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.830
No, this monstrosity is even beyond that!

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:26.750
It avoided that?! But it's so huge!
It must be even faster than the Iguazu!

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:32.670
But Mr. Bors and his group are still here,
and so is Ms. Ryu!

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.750
Running is NOT an option!

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.130
Mr. Cranel!

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.790
Fine! Let's see how it handles this!

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:48.130
FIRE...

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:48.880
No! Don't!

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.080
BOLT!

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.000
Wh-what just happened...?

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:02.710
Not good!

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.460
I have to counter!

